---
source: https://minimalistbaker.com/vegan-garlic-mashed-cauliflower/
serves: 6
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
total time: 30 minutes
---

Cut @cauliflower{2%heads} into even florets and steam in a large #pot{} with a #steamer basket{} (covered) until very tender, about 15 to ~{20%minutes} depending on size of pot and cauliflower florets. Remove from heat and set aside uncovered to cool slightly.

In the meantime, sauté @garlic{4%cloves} (3 to 4 cloves, minced) in @vegan butter{4%Tbsp} (or olive oil) in a small #skillet{} over medium-low heat for 2 to ~{3%minutes} or until just slightly browned (be careful not to burn). Or, keep the garlic raw for a punchier, stronger garlic flavor. Turn off heat and set aside.

Transfer half of the cauliflower to a #food processor{} (or use an #immersion blender{} to purée cauliflower in a pot or #saucepan{}) and process until puréed. The amount of cauliflower you can purée at once will vary based on the size of your food processor. Add half of the garlic butter as well as half of the @sea salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1%pinch} and process until well combined.

Taste and adjust flavor as needed, adding more salt and pepper to taste, garlic for intense garlic flavor, vegan butter for buttery flavor, or @unsweetened plain almond milk{1/4%cup} (up to 1/2 cup) to help the cauliflower purée. Note: You could even blend in a little nutritional yeast to add cheesy flavor, or vegan cream cheese for more creaminess (optional).

Transfer to a #mixing bowl{} or #serving platter{} and cover to keep warm. Repeat this blending and seasoning process until all the cauliflower is whipped and seasoned.

Garnish with @fresh parsley or chives{} and @vegan parmesan cheese{} (optional), and another sprinkle of salt and pepper and serve hot. Store leftovers covered in the refrigerator up to 3 to 4 days, or 1 month in the freezer. Reheat in the microwave or on the stovetop in a saucepan until hot.
